  <h2>Documented chair families</h2>
  <p>Plank, Wood, Red Wooden, Integrated, Elegant Wooden, Parsons, Slat-back, and Royal.</p>
  <h2>Reported furniture effect</h2>
  <p>Public shop dialogue describes better tables and chairs as improving tip chance and reducing the chance that customers leave. No exact percentage or guaranteed outcome is publicly established.</p>
  <h2>What is known</h2>
  <ul><li>Eight chair-family names are retained in public community documentation.</li><li>Chairs are part of the restaurant furniture system.</li><li>Public shop dialogue associates better dining furniture with tip chance and customer retention.</li></ul>
  <h2>What is not yet confirmed</h2>
  <ul><li>Current purchase and resale values for each chair</li><li>Unlock order and requirements</li><li>Exact tip-chance or customer-retention percentages</li><li>Whether every family remains available in the current shop rotation</li></ul>
